A||N||5||pherder||How to make the Fiero Speedometer work with late model Transaxle?||||5||
Z||000000||pherder||09-16-2000||05:41 PM||||Like the title states ... I am now having a problem getting my Fiero's speedo to work with the signal coming from the HO Quad 4's ECM.  <P>At first, I wasn't even getting the ECM to read the VSS until I swapped the wires.  It  seems everything I do is backwards!  Wiring diagrams state this plug with A and B outputs go to the ECM with A going one place and B going to the other.  Simple right?  That is the way I had it but got no VSS signal to the ECM (scanner shows 0 mph).  I then traded the wires (A going where B is etc.) and NOW the ECM reads mph!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>So my question is, what is everyone else using to make the Fiero's speedo work with the later model transaxles with your Northstars, 3800, etc. (assuming you are NOT using the Fiero's transaxle since then I could use existing wiring for the speedo.)<P>I have the circuit diagram that Joe Wynmann described in Fiero Owner magazine (FOCOA) but it doesn't work for me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||09-16-2000||07:33 PM||||BTW, I just hooked up a VDO electronic speedo to the ECM's output and it works so I know that the ECM is working.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Now I will have to swap out the Fiero's speedo to see if that is the problem.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||09-16-2000||08:06 PM||||Paul, I'm not sure which diagram you're looking at, but in a Fiero, the VSS signal first goes to the VSS buffer which is built into the speedometer. The buffer splits the signal and sends it to the speedometer, the odometer, cruise control, and to the ECM. If you ran the VSS wires directly to the ECM, thats your problem. The VSS violet and yellow wires go to the speedometer, and from there a brown wire feeds the ECM.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||09-16-2000||08:41 PM||||Well, I did it again   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">  Wired the signal converter circuit up backwards so when I hooked it up correctly, WAHLA!!!  Functional speedo!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Rockcrawl describes the way the Fiero gets it's signal to run the speedo.  I have a different VSS sensor and a different way the VSS signal HAS to be run for the engine to run correctly.<P>The VSS sends the signal directly to the ECM where the ECM buffers the signal and sends it to the speedo (just the opposite of how the Fiero does.)  IAW Joe Wynmann's article in FOCOA's <B>Fiero Owner</B>, The signal that comes out of the ECM is "... a square wave that consists of a primary frequency with the first five harmonics algebraically added onto that primay frequency."  What is needed to make the Fiero speedo work is a signal convertor.  "The convertor adds in the required 12 volt bias voltage to the Fiero speedometer and essentially lets only the primary desired frequency through."<P>This signal convertor is only three components!  Two resistors (22 K ohm and a 1 K ohm) and a capacitor (0.1 uf).  And if hooked up the right way ...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> ... works wonderfully!!!<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 09-16-2000).]||||reg||11
